  "analysis": "Key insight: `dd` successfully wrote 200MB to /app even though `df` reports 0 available — meaning the '100% full' is a misleading statvfs report from fuse-overlayfs, NOT a real write limit. The apt install failed only because of apt's pre-flight free-space check (Acquire::Check-Free-Space), not an actual inability to write. So I just need to bypass that check. gcc installation will pull ~71MB download + ~221MB installed, which the writable layer can clearly handle.",
  "plan": "Install gcc make wget (gcov ships with gcc; tcl isn't needed to build the SQLite shell) using `-o Acquire::Check-Free-Space=false` to bypass the false space check. I'll poll for completion. Then verify gcc/gcov are present.",
