    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get -o Acquire::Check-Free-Space=false install -y gcc make wget 2>&1 | tail -8\n",
      "duration": 30.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The `Acquire::Check-Free-Space=false` flag didn't suppress the check — apt still refuses due to its statvfs-based free-space pre-flight on /var/cache/apt/archives. However, I proved the writable layer can actually absorb 200MB of writes; the '0 avail' is a misleading statvfs report. The cleanest fix is to point apt's archive cache to the real tmpfs at /sys/fs/cgroup (32G real available), where statvfs reports genuine free space, bypassing the false check. gcc/gcov will install to / (which has real write capacity).",
