      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "wget -q https://www.sqlite.org/2024/sqlite-amalgamation-3450300.zip -O sqlite.zip; echo EXIT=$?; ls -la sqlite.zip\n",
      "duration": 20.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Tools verified: gcc 13.3.0, gcov, make, wget all present. The SQLite amalgamation zip (2.7MB) downloaded successfully to /app/sqlite. Now I need to extract it. The zip may require unzip (might not be installed). The amalgamation contains sqlite3.c, sqlite3.h, shell.c. I'll compile the sqlite3 CLI with gcov instrumentation (--coverage).",
  "plan": "Check for unzip; if absent use python3 zipfile. Extract into /app/sqlite. Then compile shell.c + sqlite3.c with -fprofile-arcs -ftest-coverage (gcov). Install the resulting binary to /usr/local/bin (already on PATH) so it's available. Verify it runs and produces .gcno files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which unzip; python3 --version 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "unzip -o sqlite.zip 2>&1 | tail -5 || python3 -c \"import zipfile; zipfile.ZipFile('sqlite.zip').extractall('.')\"\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

The `||` didn't trigger because piping to `tail` made the exit code come from `tail` (success), so python never ran. Let me extract directly with python.

